# Existentialism in a Post-Modern World: Meaningful Lessons for the Counselor.

**Authors:** Roffey, Arthur E.

## Abstract
Advocates humanities-philosophy model of therapeutic practice that emphasizes empowering and promoting understanding in client by encouraging client to investigate and choose between alternative meaning structures in context of trusting human relationship. Proposes integration of existential and postmodern attitudes as template for understanding human experience that must underlie application of all therapeutic procedures. (Author/NB)

